    "created_at": "2021-04-05T22:09:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-05T22:09:35Z",
    "body": "IMO the greatest value we could add here, as @annevk said back in 2018, is to provide a shared algorithm for extracting \"image data\" from every possible source. Then specifications could all reference the same algorithm and get uniform behavior.\r\n\r\nThe relevant sections of HTML would be:\r\n\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-createimagebitmap\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#image-sources-for-2d-rendering-contexts\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-context-2d-drawimage\r\n\r\nalthough these already depart enough from each other that I wonder if unification is really possible. (E.g. createImageBitmap given a video element rejects iff networkState = NETWORK_EMPTY, whereas drawImage() rejects iff readyState = HAVE_NOTHING or HAVE_METADATA.)\r\n\r\nCreating such an algorithm would require a good bit of refactoring and design to make sure it can be usable by all consumers. E.g. createImageBitmap takes a bunch of options: orientation, premuliply alpha, color space conversion, resize control, and cropping. drawImage takes source x/y/width/height and dest x/y/width/height. And other specs probably have their own options. The shared algorithm would need to accept all such possibilities. It'd be a good bit of work.\r\n\r\nI'd envision the shared algorithm being of the form (source, options) -> (raw pixel data in some format, origin-clean flag indicating whether it is safe to expose that pixel data to user code). Although I'm unsure how it'd handle sync vs. async considerations, e.g. reading from a Blob (for createImageBitmap) should be async but drawImage (which doesn't accept blobs) needs sync.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
