    "created_at": "2021-04-05T23:38:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-05T23:38:53Z",
    "body": "> Although I'm unsure how it'd handle sync vs. async considerations, e.g. reading from a Blob (for createImageBitmap) should be async but drawImage (which doesn't accept blobs) needs sync.\r\n\r\nFWIW, only Blob's \"image data\" can be extracted asynchronously, in any API.  \r\nA canvas could have new drawings coming right after the call to extract, or in the case of webgl the drawing buffer could get swiped, an HTMLOrSVGImageElement could have its source *image* changed, an HTMLVideoElement will probably have its current frame changed, an ImageData could have its buffer written to, an ImageBitmap (and I think a VideoFrame) can be closed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
